summary: Verifies trace is provided after system crash.
description: |
    Verifies trace is provided after system crash.
    Also confirms that setting panic=1 in cmdline causes kernel to reboot after panic.
    Test Inputs:
        trigger, echo c > /proc/sysrq-trigger
        check, validators inspect after test completion if console contains trace.
    Expected results:
        [   PASS   ] :: Command 'change_cmdline panic=1' (Expected 0, got 0)
        [   PASS   ] :: Command 'change_cmdline -panic=1' (Expected 0, got 0)
        OVERALL RESULT: PASS (/misc/crash-sysrqc/crash_sysrqc)
    Results location:
        output.txt
contact: Stephen Bertram <sbertram@redhat.com>
id: 11e4e965-18f4-41c4-9c49-472246e7d1c7
component:
  - kernel
test: bash ./runtest.sh
framework: beakerlib
require:
  - type: file
    pattern:
      - /kernel-include
      - /cki_lib
      - /cmdline_helper
recommend:
  - abootimg
  - grubby
restart-on-exit-code:
    - 255
restart-max-count: 3
duration: 30m
